[8] approach to the exceptional edge E: p = (1/2, 1-x, 0, 0), which is IN Riv+ for
    every fixed x > 0.  The finite-eps margin is -eps/(eps + (1-2eps)x); the limit is 0 only
    once eps << x, which is why a point at distance 1e-9 from E is still 'seen' as a
    non-rival at eps = 1e-10.  This is clause (9c), not a failure of the closed form.
