[9] smallest non-zero |w_DC - w_CD| over the full grid x 16 co-players.
    A float difference of two O(1) stationary probabilities carries absolute error ~1e-16,
    so any float value below that is pure noise: the raw float minimum (~1e-26) is in fact a
    pair whose exact margin is 0 (p = 0001 against q = 0001, i.e. self-play).  Below, the 400
    smallest float candidates are recomputed in exact Fractions.  The value reported is therefore
    a CERTIFIED non-zero margin and an UPPER BOUND on the true minimum -- float cannot rank
    quantities this small, so it cannot certify that no smaller one exists elsewhere.
    (Cross-checked with mpmath at dps=200 on the exact double inputs: agrees to 20 digits.)
    eps=1e-10  of the 400 smallest float candidates, 68 are EXACTLY zero;
              smallest exactly non-zero |w_DC - w_CD| = 3.426614e-37
              attained at p = (0.1, 0.0, 1.0, 0.9) vs q = 1010
    eps=1e-12  of the 400 smallest float candidates, 53 are EXACTLY zero;
              smallest exactly non-zero |w_DC - w_CD| = 3.426614e-41
              attained at p = (0.1, 0.0, 1.0, 0.9) vs q = 1010

